What this prototype doesn't do

It doesn't verify tutors. Right now anyone can add a tutor. In the real platform, every tutor would need to upload their qualifications and have them checked before they appear. Without that, the profiles are the weakest thing on the site.

It doesn't send messages or alerts. The alerts show in the browser. A real app would send them by email and by push notification, which means a backend and a way to reach the user's phone.

It doesn't take payment. The booking is confirmed, but nothing is charged.

There's one bug in the prototype. The message modal closes when you click outside it. That's a little annoying, and it's a few lines of code to fix.

